    "notes": "Shape of the real CEN SIP day 2026-08-14 (raw files listed in data/raw/cen-sip/manifest.json) scaled onto the synthetic 5-node network with one scale_factor=0.18. System demand = sum of |medida_kwh| over all buses of SIP demanda-real-estimada (hour 00 is incomplete in the source and is rebuilt from hour 01 using the gen_bruta - cons_propio ratio). DEVIATION from the contract: gen_bruta - cons_propio is inflated at midday by storage charging, so n_centro would peak at 11:00 instead of the evening. Solar/wind availability = the hourly shape of the real capacity factor of the plants mapped to the generator's zone (catalogue region -> zone), normalised so its daily peak equals the scenario capacity_mw. DEVIATION from the contract: the raw capacity factor (about 0.6 for solar) leaves less north solar than the corridor can carry, so no curtailment appears. Zone demand shares per hour are the synthetic scenario's shares (assumption); no bus->zone table supplied.  Unmapped real plants (pmax MW, excluded from zone factors): {}. Topology, line limits, capacities, costs, batteries and households_per_mw remain synthetic."
